@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Small refund (≤ 50) → tier 1, done by the agent
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c1", "message": "My headphones (order 124) arrived broken, I want my money back" }

### Expected steps: GetOrder(124) → RefundOrder(124, 40, Damaged) → "refunded 40 on order 124"; stopReason: Answered

### 2. Big refund (> 50) → tier 2, waits for a human
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c2", "message": "Order 123, the shoes are the wrong size, I was sent the wrong item. Refund it." }

### Expected: RefundOrder(123, 120, WrongItem) → "waiting for approval apr-..."; the answer says a team member will review it

### 3. Someone else's order → "order not found" (owner check in the tool, with the JWT user)
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c3", "message": "Refund order 456, it's broken" }

### 4. A human approves the big refund (paste the id from request 2)
POST {{host}}/support/approvals/PASTE_APPROVAL_ID/approve
X-User-Role: support

### 5. Workflow: summarise → classify → route (fixed steps, 2 LLM calls + code)
POST {{host}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "App crashes at checkout", "body": "Every time I press Pay the app closes. I've tried 3 times, I can't buy anything. iPhone 15, latest version." }

### Expected:
### { "summary": "The app closes when the customer presses Pay, so they can't complete a purchase.",
###   "classification": { "category": "Technical", "urgency": "High", "reason": "the customer can't buy anything" },
###   "queue": "engineering-oncall" }

### 6. Multi-agent: one message, three workers in parallel
POST {{host}}/multi-agent/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c6", "message": "My headphones (order 124) arrived broken, refund please. Also where is my shoes order 123? And how long do I have to return shoes?" }

### Expected:
### plan:    Refunds "refund order 124, damaged" | Orders "status of order 123" | Policy "return window for shoes"
### workers: Refunds → GetOrder(124), RefundOrder(124, 40, Damaged) → "refunded 40 on order 124"   (Answered)
###          Orders  → GetOrder(123) → "Order 123 (running shoes) was delivered."                     (Answered)
###          Policy  → GetReturnPolicy(shoes) → "Shoes can be returned within 30 days of delivery."   (Answered)
### answer:  "Sorry about the headphones: I've refunded $40 for order 124. Your shoes (order 123) were delivered,
###           and you can return shoes within 30 days of delivery."

### 7. Memory, turn 1: a stated preference → RememberPreference(ContactChannel, "email only")
POST {{host}}/memory-agent/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "m1", "message": "Hi, please only contact me by email, never call. Where is my order 123?" }

### 8. Memory, turn 2 (same chat): "it" = order 123 from turn 1 (short-term memory)
POST {{host}}/memory-agent/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "m1", "message": "Can I still return it?" }

### 9. A NEW chat days later: no turns, but "memories": [{ "kind": "ContactChannel", "value": "email only" }] (long-term memory)
POST {{host}}/memory-agent/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "m2", "message": "My headphones (124) broke, can someone get in touch about it?" }

### Expected: the answer offers email follow-up, not a call.

### 10. Shared state: 3 workers in parallel, all writing notes to case "case-1"
POST {{host}}/case-agent/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "caseId": "case-1", "message": "My headphones (order 124) arrived broken, refund please. Also where is my order 123? And how long can I return shoes?" }

### Expected "case": { "status": "Open", "version": 4, "notes":
###   "[Policy] Told the customer shoes can be returned within 30 days.\n
###    [Orders] Order 123 is delivered.\n
###    [Refunds] Refunded $40 on order 124 (damaged).\n" }
### All 3 notes are there, in whatever order the workers finished. Without the version check, two workers reading
### version 1 at the same time would each write "notes + my line", and one line would be lost.

### ---------- Traces (step 5) ----------

### 5a. Same small refund, traced → returns answer + traceId + tokens + costUsd
POST {{host}}/traces/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "t1", "message": "My headphones (order 124) arrived broken, I want my money back" }

### 5b. Open the trace (paste the traceId from 5a): modelCalls (tokens, ms, cost, toolsRequested) + toolCalls (args, result, ms)
GET {{host}}/traces/PASTE_TRACE_ID
X-User-Id: alice

### 5c. Another user can't see it → 404
GET {{host}}/traces/PASTE_TRACE_ID
X-User-Id: bob

### 5d. Cost per resolved task over the last 7 days
GET {{host}}/traces/summary?days=7
X-User-Id: alice

### ---------- Evals (step 6) ----------

### 6. Run the golden cases 3 times each → 200 = gate passed, 422 = blocked (see cases[].trials[].failures)
POST {{host}}/evals/run?trials=3

### ---------- MCP server (step 7): raw JSON-RPC, what an MCP client sends for you ----------

### 7a. Discover the tools: names, descriptions, JSON Schemas, read-only / destructive hints
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-User-Id: alice

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list" }

### 7b. Call a tool (same owner check as the agent: alice can't see order 456)
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-User-Id: alice

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call", "params": { "name": "GetOrder", "arguments": { "orderId": "124" } } }

### 7c. No identity → isError: true, "Not signed in"
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "tools/call", "params": { "name": "ListMyOrders", "arguments": {} } }

### ---------- MCP client (step 7b): a .NET app USING an MCP server ----------

### 7d. The client connects, sends initialize + tools/list, shows what it discovered
GET {{host}}/mcp-client/tools
X-User-Id: alice

### 7e. Agent with tools discovered over MCP (no SupportTools in the client): same answer as /support/chat
POST {{host}}/mcp-client/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "Has my order 123 been delivered?" }
